From 56af2892b7f9d6f3af2bc88a75177a1e3033e891 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 15:25:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 113/121] P19 stage B: P24 wave plan over the whole layer pool,
 P26 (a)/(b) graph inputs on the card, input-cost probes (lab L034-L039)

All under environment variables, off by default; byte for byte at 48K (exact and default, k 1 and 4) against the
normal path (SiegeLadder runs 4.295-4.299).
- L039 LLAMA_DSV4_LAYER_MAJOR_POOL_PLAN=pool: the P11 wave plan sees the whole layer pool (384 slots, 2 waves per layer
  instead of ~14.5); shrink and call end return it to the base. 512K 508.65 -> 691.22 tok/s, 1.42x the normal path.
- L037 GGML_OP_PREFIX_MASK (last in the enum, CPU and CUDA) + LLAMA_DSV4_MASK_GPU=1: the compressed-KV masks are built
  on the device from n_visible; the lead pins the PREFIX_MASK nodes to backend 0 (the scheduler left them on the CPU).
- L038 LLAMA_DSV4_LAYER_MAJOR_PIPE=1: the H carry input lives in a CUDA buffer outside the allocator; with
  L035 LLAMA_DSV4_LAYER_MAJOR_CARRY_ASYNC=1 it is filled on the graph's stream (carry_in 5.9 -> 0.17 ms per graph).
- L034 LLAMA_DSV4_LAYER_MAJOR_INPUT_CACHE=1|2 (mask cache, not to be enabled) and per-tensor input cost lines under
  LLAMA_DSV4_LAYER_MAJOR_COST=2.
- L036 test-backend-ops MUL_MAT_ID perf cases (384 experts, 6 used, uniform ids) for P25.
